Close pyplot figures between tests

pydefect's Mpl plotters draw onto pyplot's *current* axes rather than onto one
they create.  `SitePotentialMplPlotter.construct_plot` is the clearest case:

    def construct_plot(self):
        self._add_potentials()
        ...

    def _add_potentials(self):
        ...
        self.plt.scatter(distances, potentials, marker="o", color=color, ...)

There is no `plt.figure()` anywhere in it, so `scatter` goes to whatever
`gca()` returns.  That is the normal matplotlib scripting contract and is not a
bug in the library — but nothing in the suite ever closes a figure, so one test
inherits the axes the last one left behind.

When the survivor is `chem_pot_diag/cpd_plotter.py`'s three-dimensional
diagram, the next plotting test dies:

    self = <Axes3D: title={'center': 'Chemical potential diagram of H-O-N'},
            xlabel='Chemical potential of H', ...>
    s = masked_array(data=[None], ..., dtype=object)
    E   ValueError: s must be float, but has type object

`Axes3D.scatter` declares `s=None` and forwards it to `Axes.scatter`, where a
2-D axes would have substituted the rcParam default.  So the failure is not
about marker sizes at all: it is a 3-D axes receiving a 2-D plot.

This is order-dependent, which means it is also a lottery under pytest-xdist —
which test lands on which worker decides whether it fires at all.  Closing
every figure after each test removes the shared state rather than the symptom,
and leaves each plotter to get the fresh 2-D axes it expects.

--- a/pydefect/tests/conftest.py
+++ b/pydefect/tests/conftest.py
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 from math import sqrt
 from pathlib import Path
 
+import matplotlib.pyplot
 import pytest
 from pydefect.analyzer.defect_energy import DefectEnergies, DefectEnergy, \
     DefectEnergySummary
@@ -24,6 +25,17 @@
 # Need the following to share the fixture
 
 
+@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
+def _close_pyplot_figures():
+    """Leave no figure current for the next test.
+
+    The Mpl plotters draw onto ``plt.gca()``, so a figure surviving one test is
+    inherited by the one after it.
+    """
+    yield
+    matplotlib.pyplot.close("all")
+
+
 @pytest.fixture(scope="session")
 def test_data_files():
     return Path(__file__).parent / "test_data_files"
